Comments:       UPGRADE WARNING this TCE is now a dep of
                audacious-plugins. If this TCE is in your boot 
                list change it to audacious-plugins.tcz

                No fuss audio.... pulldown File Settings Audio 
                pulldown audio plugin and choose sdl2
                -> playback should work with no further setup
                alsa or pulseaudio plugins assumes setup. 
                filewriter is not a playback plugin its a write plugin

                To play cd -> Services -> play cd
                See doc info for keybindings 
                
                Some common issues discussed here
                https://audacious-media-player.org/problems

                Optional TCES 
                faad2 for aac file formats
                See streaming or add curl neon mpg123 wavpack opusfile 
                
                Streaming sites (URL)
                ############### If its a true audio URL, mpg123 should stream it. 
                I suggest you bookmark this list of 1196 audio streams by Axel Schneider
                but contains some 404 = stale links
                https://gist.github.com/Axel-Erfurt/3b1965ac233f65a4f968a649c7ae40bf
                
                ERROR=unknown URI scheme is resolved by loading curl and neon
                ERROR=unknown plugin -> close gui open a terminal and run audacious again
                with your target URL, you will see which shared object(s) you are missing 
                eg number 63, I was missing libmpg123.so.0 -> load mpg123 
                Always exit the GUI and restart it to start streaming if you have loaded TCES
                If still error + no more shared objects show up, URL is stale or incomplete             
                
                audtool is CLI player
                                
